 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271705 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271705 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186270684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271705 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6c4e3630-6513-56c7-9a3b-beeebecf2727" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186271278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271888 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271888 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271888 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186269833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271888 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d5425c9e-f9a3-50d1-b38c-a404e2f613e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271995 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271995 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139989" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271995 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271995 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y-2z &=-7 \\\\ 2x+y-4z &=-10 \\\\ 3x-3y-2z &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $16,$ then $z=$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186271995 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e8e68a9-7d99-5bc1-967a-dd0267847130" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271995 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+(-5)y+(-2z) &=-7 \\\\ 2x+1y+(-4)z &=-10 \\\\ 3x+(-3)y+(-2)z &=-7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ -3 & -7\\end{aligned}|-(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{aligned}|+(-7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-7-30)+5(-14+30)-7(-6-3) \\\\  & =-111+80+63 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{32}{16}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186272007 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272007 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140042" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272007 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272007 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y-5z &=1 \\\\ 2x+3y-3z &=k \\\\ -5x+3y+7z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that $y=-1$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-19,$ find the value of $k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186272007 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b99085c9-ade3-5f37-a123-f7c001cf1137" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272007 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|=-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -3 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -3 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}|+(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(7k-6)-(14-15)-5(-4+5k) \\\\  & =21k-18+1+20-25k \\\\  & =-4k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{-4k+3}{-19}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $y=-1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4k+3}{-19} & =-1 \\\\ -4k+3 & =19 \\\\ -4k & =16 \\\\ k & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327044 #edb/ref 1080 "k=5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327044 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327044 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0cce91bb-3f2d-594d-b001-b74e585728b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327418 #edb/ref 1080 "k=-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327418 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327418 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37c36c30-f71a-5c42-8e1f-9edf8e05698a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327488 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327488 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327488 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f3c771f-c51e-5841-8533-1a9671c2d6cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327529 #edb/ref 1080 "k=-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327529 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327529 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "44045eca-a7ba-59e9-8fbf-163cca4eb93a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327717 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327717 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327717 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "596aae9d-1263-5f81-8c32-fcfac678f572" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328428 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328428 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328428 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ac1518da-c8dd-5fdb-b4cb-d1e5e1748f89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328994 #edb/ref 1080 "k=-9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328994 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921